      "recommendation": "Start beginners at the lower end of weekly hard sets and progress mainly through reps and load; start experienced users at higher weekly sets with closer RIR targets and slower expected progress.",
      "evidenceStrength": "Moderate that trained lifters grow more slowly (consistent across trials and meta-analyses), though Ahtiainen 2003 is small (n=16). How much starting volume should differ by experience has not been tested directly; the starting-set numbers are a programming convention. Years of experience show little effect on RIR accuracy; repeated practice improved it in two short trials, though one small trial in trained lifters found no change.",
